{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 10, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "## Lost in Translation (and Loving It!) - My Japan Adventure\n\nJapan. The word itself conjures images of ancient temples, bustling cityscapes, and serene gardens. And let me tell you, it lived up to every expectation – and then some! \n\nMy recent trip was a whirlwind of sensory overload. From the moment I stepped off the plane in Tokyo, I was captivated. The neon lights of Shibuya Crossing were breathtaking, a chaotic yet strangely organized spectacle.  I spent hours wandering through the vibrant markets of Tsukiji, sampling everything from fresh seafood to quirky street food. \n\nBut it wasn’t just the cities.  I took a bullet train to Kyoto, a city steeped in history.  Visiting Fushimi Inari Shrine with its thousands of vibrant red torii gates was truly magical.  The peaceful bamboo forest of Arashiyama was a welcome escape from the urban energy. \n\nThe people were incredibly kind and helpful, even with my limited Japanese.  Simple gestures like bowing and offering a smile went a long way.  And the food?  Oh, the food!  Ramen, sushi, tempura – I ate my way through Japan and didn't regret a single bite.\n\nIt was a trip that challenged me, delighted me, and left me wanting more.  Japan is a country of contrasts, of tradition and modernity, and it’s a place that truly gets under your skin.  If you're looking for an adventure, I can't recommend it enough.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0021045696921646595}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": -0.1269848495721817}, {"token": "▁Translation", "logprob": -0.0005858612130396068}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.3485564589500427}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -0.0006665153778158128}, {"token": "▁Loving", "logprob": -0.0003225283289793879}, {"token": "▁It", "logprob": -0.00034433635300956666}, {"token": "!)", "logprob": -0.30323243141174316}, {"token": "▁-", "logp